#===============================================================
# SampClen_V1_2_PUBLIC.r
#
# Purpose:
#   R version of SampClen. Splits a fixed-width sample file into
#   a GOOD file and a BAD file using run-time options (DNC, PCI,
#   invalid area codes, toll free, AK/HI, Canadian, etc.).
#   Built for very large files (1.9 million+ phones).
#
# Inputs:
#   1. Fixed-width sample file (.txt or .dat)
#   2. Sampling Layout Utility report
#      (typically Printed_Samplay.txt)
#   3. Lists for the options that are checked:
#        DNC            dontcall.txt
#        Wireless DNC   (path selected by user)
#        PCI Purge      pci purge.TXT
#        Used file      (path selected by user)
#        Valid area     AreaCodeListing.TXT
#        Toll free      800.TXT
#        AK / HI        akhi.TXT
#        Canadian       canada.TXT
#
# Output (two fixed-width files):
#   GOOD file   records that passed every check, exactly as read
#   BAD file    records removed by any check, written as:
#                 [2-digit reason code][one space][original record]
#               so every field in the BAD file is pushed right 3
#               columns. Example (DNC):
#                 05 6105551212...
#   The summary (counts by reason) is shown on the screen and in
#   the R console.
#
# Reason codes (first reason that removes a record is used):
#   01  Invalid digits (phone is not exactly 10 digits)
#   02  Invalid area code
#   03  Duplicate within this file
#   04  Duplicate with previous (used file)
#   05  DNC / Wireless DNC / PCI Purge
#   06  Toll free
#   07  AK / HI
#   08  Canadian area code
#   (06-08 are not in the original list; change STEP_CODE below)
#
# Rules:
#   - The phone field position comes from the layout report
#   - Removal steps run in this order and each record is counted
#     once, under the FIRST reason that removes it:
#       1 DNC   2 Wireless DNC   3 PCI   4 Used   5 Invalid numerics
#       6 Toll free   7 AK/HI   8 Canadian   9 Invalid area codes
#       10 Duplicates within this file
#   - Invalid numeric = phone is not exactly 10 digits
#   - DNC / PCI / Wireless / Used lists: first value on each line
#     is the phone; non-digits are removed; a leading 1 on an
#     11-digit number is dropped
#   - Area-code lists: one 3-digit area code per line
#   - Duplicates: the first record is kept, later ones removed
#   - GOOD records are written exactly as read
#
# Features:
#   - Layout driven (no hard-coded positions)
#   - Always-on-top Tcl/Tk run-time options window
#   - Large-file friendly: records are streamed in chunks; only
#     the phone numbers are held in memory
#
# Version History:
#   V1    First R version of SampClen
#   V1.1  Two outputs: GOOD file and BAD file (fixed-width)
#   V1.2  Reason code + space added at the start of each BAD record
#
# Author:
#   Phil Benner
#===============================================================

